  "goodToKnow": "Das Debüt is a debut: ihr Debüt als Regisseurin, das Debütalbum, der Debütroman. It comes from French début, so many Germans drop the t: de-BÜ, though de-BÜT is also heard. Der Debütant (die Debütantin) is a newcomer, and der Debütantinnenball is a debutante ball, still held at the Vienna Opera Ball. Debütieren means to make one's debut. Plural: die Debüts."
